# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# One rule per line: <from> <to> <status>. Evaluated top to bottom, first match
# wins. Query strings are ignored when matching and preserved on the redirect,
# so /account?mode=login is covered by the /account rule.
#
# /learn.html -> /learn needs no rule here: Pages already 308s extensionless
# paths natively (verified 2026-09-06).

# --- Fake auth system removed -----------------------------------------------
# /account was a genuine live 200 serving a signup/login form with no backend.
# /login and /signup were soft-404s serving the homepage, so they may be
# indexed as homepage duplicates. Consolidate all three onto /.
/account           /                      301
/account/*         /                      301
/login             /                      301
/signup            /                      301

# --- Aliases the old dev server mapped and site.js linked to ----------------
# Both were soft-404s in production, not real pages.
/home              /                      301
/partner-program   /partner               301

# --- Consolidated in the Astro rebuild --------------------------------------
# /learn and /knowledge-hub were two overlapping index pages: /learn advertised
# 42 lessons that did not exist, /knowledge-hub listed nine teasers pointing
# back at the same guides. One index at /guides replaces both.
/learn               /guides                301
/knowledge-hub       /guides                301
/alice-blue-partner  /partner               301

# --- Assets from the pre-Astro site ----------------------------------------
# The 334KB logo PNG is the only one plausibly hotlinked from elsewhere; the
# stylesheet and scripts were subresources of pages that no longer exist, so a
# 404 is the correct answer for those.
/assets/moneygoal-logo.png  /favicon.svg  301

# --- The committed dist/ directory was published at the repo root -----------
# Every page had a complete duplicate: /dist/learn returned 200 with the full
# 56,040-byte page and no canonical tag. Collapse the tree onto the real URL.
#
# The three consolidated URLs are listed before the splat so they resolve in ONE
# hop — /dist/learn -> /guides, not /dist/learn -> /learn -> /guides. First
# match wins, so the order of these four lines is load-bearing.
/dist/learn               /guides    301
/dist/knowledge-hub       /guides    301
/dist/alice-blue-partner  /partner   301
/dist/*                   /:splat    301
